[issue_comment] lucasdemarchi | created=2017-07-12T07:59:39Z | updated=2017-07-12T07:59:39Z | https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/pull/6501#issuecomment-314686589
LGTM. I guess we should use the time conversion macros here, too. It would be like this:

```c++
uint64_t AP_HAL::Util::set_system_clock(uint64_t time_utc_usec) const
{
    timespec ts{};

    ts.tv_sec = time_utc_usec / AP_USEC_PER_SEC;
    ts.tv_nsec = (time_utc_usec % AP_USEC_PER_SEC) * AP_NSEC_PER_USEC;

    clock_settime(CLOCK_REALTIME, &ts);
}
```

And get_system_clock():
```c++
uint64_t AP_HAL::Util::get_system_clock_ms() const
{
#if defined(__APPLE__) && defined(__MACH__)
    struct timeval ts;
    gettimeofday(&ts, nullptr);

    return (uint64_t) ts.tv_sec * AP_MSEC_PER_SEC +
           (uint64_t) ts.tv_usec / AP_USEC_PER_MSEC;
#else
    struct timespec ts;
    clock_gettime(CLOCK_REALTIME, &ts);

    return (uint64_t) ts.tv_sec * AP_MSEC_PER_SEC +
           (uint64_t) ts.tv_nsec / AP_NSEC_PER_MSEC;
#endif
}
```

