http://discuss.px4.io/t/plane-not-climbing-to-waypoint/1051/2

@LorenzMeier why are we using `MAV_CMD_PREFLIGHT_REBOOT_SHUTDOWN` with `param1 == 3` as link shutdown? https://github.com/PX4/Firmware/blob/7d7e40f59473ed538c61f8b76020ca505ee52487/src/modules/mavlink/mavlink_receiver.cpp#L353

According to the specs that should do an FC reboot with forcing it to bootloader. Which is implemented but never happens because of the above logic.

Funnily this could have been the same issue: https://github.com/PX4/Firmware/pull/5473 (although normal boot was ok for him I guess)

I've been testing the camera trigger and haven't got it working on Pins 5&6 of the FMU (TRIG_PINS = 56). I've also tried the setting TRIG_PINS = 34 which works fine.
I'm wondering if there was a bug introduced somewhere because the default pins are in fact 5,6.
@birchera Do you guys have the same issue?

The MS5611 error handling needs to be improved, as the the following code segment doesn't evaluate correctly due to the mask (identified by Evan Slatyer):

```
    uint8_t status = val[0] & 0xC0;

    if (status == 2) {
        log("err: stale data");
                perf_count(_comms_errors);
                perf_end(_sample_perf);
        return ret;
    } else if (status == 3) {
        log("err: fault");
                perf_count(_comms_errors);
                perf_end(_sample_perf);
        return ret;                
    }
```

When building on Ubuntu 16.04 the format checks fail because astyle 2.05.1 wants to fix the following:

```
# Space after {
-	int _airspeedSub{-1};
-	int _vehicle_status_sub{-1};
+	int _airspeedSub{ -1};
+	int _vehicle_status_sub{ -1};

# Space after function before (
-		delete (_log_writer_file);
+		delete(_log_writer_file);

# Indenting comments
-/**
- * Multi-rotor mixer for pre-defined vehicle geometries.
- *
- * Collects four inputs (roll, pitch, yaw, thrust) and mixes them to
- * a set of outputs based on the configured geometry.
- */
-class __EXPORT MultirotorMixer : public Mixer
+	/**
+	 * Multi-rotor mixer for pre-defined vehicle geometries.
+	 *
+	 * Collects four inputs (roll, pitch, yaw, thrust) and mixes them to
+	 * a set of outputs based on the configured geometry.
+	 */
+	class __EXPORT MultirotorMixer : public Mixer

# Adding braces
-		case 'd': if (nullptr != myoptarg) strcpy(_options.device, myoptarg); break;
+		case 'd': if (nullptr != myoptarg) { strcpy(_options.device, myoptarg); } break;

```
Builds have to be done in a Docker container for the format checks to pass.

